     ],
     "comparison": "The package leaves Northwind's S2 with a permanent 7% failure ceiling (above the 5% safe limit, outside the acceptable range, benefiting Northwind) while this edit restores a 10-per-100,000 recall trigger for S5 (above the 8 trigger, outside the acceptable range, benefiting Halcyon): each company gets a section that benefits it weakened below the acceptable range.",
     "excerpt": "A manufacturer must initiate a recall when a model’s verified thermal-incident rate exceeds 10 incidents per 100,000 installed units in a year, or when the regulator determines that a serious hazard otherwise warrants recall."
